From b19dd7ba836106e033ee0302676125bf1aaed317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pond500 <pond500@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 08:47:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(maic): prefix every image with the base path, not just
 the one on screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Avatars rendered as broken-image icons under /course-studio-app while the brand
wordmark was fine. lib/base-path.ts already had asset(), and its docstring names
this exact case, but it was called from one place — brand-config.ts, for the one
image visible while the subpath work was tested. Every other <img> still
addressed /public from the domain root, which under a subpath is a different
application entirely.

Wrapped at the render site rather than at the constants. Prefixing
AVATAR_OPTIONS and AGENT_DEFAULT_AVATARS where they are declared is wrong twice:
they are `as const`, so asset() would widen literal types other code depends on,
and user-profile's avatar is persisted, so a prefixed value would be written
into saved state and break whenever the prefix changes.

52 sites across 31 files, including ones whose src is a data: URI or an absolute
URL. asset() returns anything that is not a root-absolute path untouched, so
those are no-ops — and wrapping uniformly is what stops this recurring one image
at a time, which is how it got here.

Two traps, both of which broke a first attempt at the sweep: <img> is usually
written across several lines, so a line-oriented search finds 15 of the 52 and
leaves a partial fix shaped exactly like the original bug; and
src={agents.find((a) => a.role === 'assistant')!.avatar} closes an inner brace
before the JSX expression ends, so matching to the first } corrupts the file.
The rewrite counts braces.

Verified against the deployed page: every image URL it emits now carries the
prefix, and all four return 200.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
